# Writer 11 (tally 2.1, 2.1-6, R-2). L §3.5: "The prelude kind parties is their root: a model declares its own
# subkinds of it (kind persons: parties, ...), or enters its parties at parties itself when it declares none"; L §5.7:
# "a binding over a kind ranges over every thing ... of that kind, its subkinds included". q counts the parties alive on
# 2026-06-30: ania and tomek (persons) and the estate e (estates, from 2026-05-01): 3; on 2026-03-01 the estate isn't
# alive: 2; persons alone: 2. q2 is a model with no subkinds that enters its parties at parties itself.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind persons: parties
kind estates: parties
ask q: count(p in parties on 2026-06-30), count(p in parties on 2026-03-01), count(p in persons on 2026-06-30)

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  persons + [ania] lives 1980-01-01..
  persons + [tomek] lives 1981-01-01..
  estates + [e] lives 2026-05-01..
=== expect
q: (3, 2, 2)
  cut 2026-01-01
